<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Rantzau</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1726 CE · capital Barmstedt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tiny Holstein county that won imperial status for the Rantzau family and ended after a fratricide.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-rantzau">Christian zu Rantzau</a>, a Danish statesman, bought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barmstedt">Barmstedt</a> from the Duke of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-holstein-gottorp">Holstein-Gottorp</a> in 1649. In 1650 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Ferdinand III</a> raised him to imperial count and made Barmstedt an immediate imperial county, outside the duchy of Holstein.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The county covered only a few villages and the market town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elmshorn">Elmshorn</a>, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barmstedt">Barmstedt</a> and a castle on an island in the Rantzau lake. Its counts enjoyed full jurisdiction but depended on their Danish connections. In 1721 Count Christian Detlev was shot dead, and his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-adolf-count-of-rantzau">Wilhelm Adolf</a> was arrested and convicted of arranging the killing.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-adolf-count-of-rantzau">Wilhelm Adolf</a> died in prison in 1734, but the Danish king had already occupied the county, and in 1726 it was annexed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> under a prior agreement, becoming a district of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-holstein">Holstein</a>. It later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/provisional-government-of-schleswig-holstein">Schleswig-Holstein</a> in 1867.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="county, 1650 CE – 1726 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">county</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:92.54%;width:1.51%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1726 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Barmstedt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Christian zu Rantzau, Christian Detlev, Wilhelm Adolf</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Low German, German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Imperial County of Rantzau</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1688&amp;focus=county-of-rantzau" aria-label="County of Rantzau on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4897 331 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Rantzau lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5217 587L5229 694M5217 587L5274 535"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5274 535h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5217 587h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5217 587h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Barmstedt. <a href="/atlas?year=1688&amp;focus=county-of-rantzau">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
